 [m³/h]\". Canonical: qmin. And \"maximum pmax [bar]\" → pmax. Diameter D [mm] → diameter.\n\nAccuracy class column → accuracy_class.\n\nG-value → g_value.\n\nVolume* V [dm³] → cyclic_volume (the footnote says see next page — likely explains V is cyclic volume per R137 terminology; I shouldn't assume; but \"cyclic_volume\" is the R137 term for V. The example in the prompt used \"cyclic_volume\" for dm³ column. I'll use \"cyclic_volume\".)\n\nNow build the JSON.\n\ncertificate:\n```json\n{\n  \"number\": \"R 137/2012-B-NL1-18.04\",\n  \"scheme\": \"B\",\n  \"project_number\": \"1901860\",\n  \"page_total\": 5,\n  \"member_state\": \"The Netherlands\",\n  \"date_issued\": \"2018-09-24\",\n  \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n}\n```\n\nissuing_authority:\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"NMi Certin B.V.\",\n  \"address_lines\": [\"Hugo de Grootplein 1\", \"3314 EG Dordrecht\", \"The Netherlands\"],\n  \"person_responsible\": \"C. Oosterman\",\n  \"person_title\": \"Head Certification Board\",\n  \"phone\": \"+31 78 6332332\",\n  \"email\": \"certin@nmi.nl\",\n  \"website\": \"www.nmi.nl\",\n  \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n}\n```\nNote the header says \"NMi Certin B.V., OIML Issuing Authority NL1\".\n\napplicants: [{name: \"Flow Meter Group B.V.\", address_lines: [\"Innovatieweg 32\", \"7007 CD Doetinchem\", \"The Netherlands\"]}]\n\nmanufacturers: same.\n\ncertified_type:\n```json\n{\n  \"category\": \"Gas meter\",\n  \"type_designations\": [\"FMR\", \"FMR-Dual\"],\n  \"module_designation\": \"Not applicable\",\n  \"description\": \"A rotary piston gas meter\"\n}\n```\n\nmodel_family: family_name \"FMR and FMR-Dual\", models 48 entries label \"FMR\".\n\nHmm — is it right to call family_name \"FMR and FMR-Dual\"? The table caption is \"General characteristics of the family of instruments (FMR and FMR-Dual)\". I'll use that.\n\ncharacteristics.type_level:\n```json\n{\n  \"destined_for_measurement\": {\"value\": \"Gas volume\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null},\n  \"mechanical